From: rcllf <noreply@rcllf.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rcllf marker for 0005-federate-discard-rti-message-past-stop

Puts the string "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0005-federate-discard-rti-message-past-stop"
into section rcllf_reactor_c_patches of every program that compiles this file.
A tool can read the section back from the running program to check that
a configured patch is present.

The hunk removes and re-adds a line that only the fix has, so it applies only on
top of the fix. The marker sits outside the fix hunk's context, so the fix patch
still reads "previously applied" on a tree that has both. federate.c is compiled
into federated programs only.

Rcllf-Marker-For: 0005-federate-discard-rti-message-past-stop
Rcllf-Marker-Scope: federated
---
--- a/core/federated/federate.c
+++ b/core/federated/federate.c
@@ -648,15 +648,22 @@
-      // Freshly allocated and never scheduled (ref_count 0): free it directly.
+      // Freshly allocated and never scheduled (ref_count 0): free it directly.
       _lf_free_token(message_token);
 #ifdef FEDERATED_DECENTRALIZED
       _lf_decrement_tag_barrier_locked(env);
 #endif
       LF_MUTEX_UNLOCK(&env->mutex);
       return 0;
     }
 
     // If the current time >= stop time, discard the message.
     // But only if the stop time is not equal to the start time!
     if (lf_tag_compare(env->current_tag, env->stop_tag) >= 0 && env->execution_started) {
+      {
+        // rcllf patch marker: the benchmark harness reads it back from the running
+        // program. The hunk also rewrites a line of the fix, so it applies only on top of it.
+        static const char rcllf_marker[]
+            __attribute__((section("rcllf_reactor_c_patches"), used, unused)) =
+            "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0005-federate-discard-rti-message-past-stop";
+      }
       lf_print_error("Received message too late. Already at stop tag.\n"
                      "    Current tag is " PRINTF_TAG " and intended tag is " PRINTF_TAG ".\n"
                      "    Discarding message and closing the network connection.",
